[00:02.49]Peeled the paint off of my fingers
[00:04.76]Picked up all the patterns, let them fall away
[00:09.77]Used to leave it 'til my skin hurt
[00:12.23]But I don't need that feeling anymore
[00:16.69]The blinding white of freshly mounted linen
[00:20.18][03:59.53]All the love and life that just needs definition
[00:23.98]And I only took it where I wanted
[00:27.26]Never where I needed, never room to change
[00:31.50][01:57.73]It’s different now
[00:33.57]The way the colors shine through, but
[00:35.92]Is the promise of tomorrow ever truly absolute?
[00:41.10]If I take the hues and combine into something new 
[00:44.36]Could it reach you too?
