[01:06.90][02:48.06]My lucky piece (To reality)
[01:08.68][02:49.98]And send a sketch of fairer fortune out
[01:11.03][02:52.35]Upon the passing breeze
[01:15.39][03:37.74] 
[01:28.59]Picked a clover from the meadow
[01:31.16]Pressed it in my journal, for a rainy day
[01:35.84]I just want to follow in your footsteps
[01:38.43]But I don't even know yet what it's like to say
[01:42.96]"I'm more than this, I'm not a perfect person,
[01:46.42]I will sing and dance and love without a purpose"
[01:50.18]But I try to get a little closer
[01:53.45]With every single brushstroke running off the page
[01:59.77]The way the colors shine through, I
[02:02.13]Used to linger waiting hopelessly for something I could prove
[02:07.29]But the wonder wasn’t something that I could choose
[02:10.54]And you knew that too, didn’t you?
[02:12.67]Is it different how
[02:14.81]The things you left behind you all
[02:17.08]Seem to shimmer in the light
[02:19.46]From a different point of view?
[02:22.35]If I falter, and I turn my sight around
[02:25.55]Would it sparkle too?
[02:56.48][04:08.51]
[03:09.00]Between the verdant touch of green
[03:12.02]The dappled sunlight casts a crown on me 
[03:16.17]And though I trip and fall 
